      "t": "Problem",
      "hidden": false,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "t": "Manual proctoring couldn't scale, and recording full sessions for thousands of simultaneous test-takers was infeasible on storage and memory.",
      "hidden": false,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "t": "Approach & key decisions",
      "hidden": false,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "t": "Defined a lightweight monitoring design with engineering — screenshots every 10 seconds, flagged against predefined malpractice patterns (multiple faces, phones in frame), feeding a human-review pipeline. Led definition of edge cases and success metrics so AI accuracy and reviewer load stayed in balance; tight AI constraints plus human oversight was the deliberate architecture.",
      "hidden": false,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "t": "Results",
      "hidden": false,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "t": "Manual proctoring cut from 100 to 30 hours per exam batch across 15,000+ exam sessions, scaled with no memory overload.",
      "hidden": false,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "t": "Specific internal data is summarised at the level Newton School permits publicly; happy to discuss details in conversation.",
      "hidden": false,
      "visible": true
